The degree-flat model still has a fatal special case: perfectly regular planting creates an exact spectral color subspace, precisely the kind of construction leak the prompt warns about. I’m avoiding that by using overlapping random matchings (same law for planted and decoy edges, but with enough collision noise to break equitable degrees) and including both spectral recovery and exact DSATUR in the adversary panel. The certificate remains construction-first: the coloring is sampled before any edge exists, then carried through the paper’s Theorem 1 reduction into a replayable schedule.
