+NOTES: str = r"""
+Definition.  Section 2, Definition 1 fixes d=2: an old vertex creates at most
+one child per slot, and the child may attach only to its parent and the old
+neighbors of that parent.  Proposition 1 then forces every set of vertices
+born in one slot to be independent in the target graph.
+
+Step 0 and hardness.  Section 4's fast-growth theorem is an explicit
+polynomial-time perfect-matching plus 2-SAT algorithm for exactly log n slots
+and zero excess, so that regime cannot be Track A.  Candidate elimination is
+also polynomial for unrestricted length n-1, and constant excess remains
+polynomial.  The family instead uses Section 4, Theorem 1: for an arbitrary G,
+join an isomorphic copy of G to a same-sized clique of universal vertices.
+The resulting graph has a zero-excess schedule with the clique prefix followed
+by q independent slots exactly when G is q-colourable.  The theorem makes the
+zero-excess decision problem NP-complete.  Worst-case hardness alone is not
+claimed as evidence for this generator's distribution: the shipping G5/G6
+measure capped exact DSATUR and a spectral partition attack on the actual
+sparse planted distribution.
+
+Construction.  A balanced three-way partition is sampled first.  For every
+pair of parts, independently shuffled perfect matchings are overlaid.  Duplicate
+edges are coalesced, creating small degree fluctuations and removing the exact
+equitable-partition eigenvector leaked by a perfectly regular construction.
+Only cross-part edges are ever inserted.  The target is the paper's join with
+K_n.  The planted colouring is canonicalised and directly describes the last
+three slots.  The universal clique grows first, one vertex per slot; each base
+vertex then uses a different universal vertex as parent.  Universal parents
+are adjacent to every old vertex, so all requested target edges are legal and
+no edge is deleted.
+
+Attacks.  Labels and class membership are independently shuffled.  Overlaying
+the same number of matchings between every pair makes degree an uninformative
+plant marker; collisions provide spectral noise.  The panel includes degree
+ranking, left-to-right greedy colouring, 256 random-order greedy restarts,
+two-vector shifted-adjacency spectral clustering, and capped exact DSATUR.
+The last is the standard exact graph-colouring attack.  A solved attack is
+reported as a failed gate; it is never hidden as a reference algorithm.
+""".strip()
