codex
The generator is now implemented in the paper’s own graph objects. Its certificate is an unordered independent-set partition that the verifier expands and replays as the full zero-excess schedule; generation samples that partition first, so no solver is hidden in `make_instance`. I’m running the full 200,000-guess test, five-attack panel, relabelling proof, and doubled-size replay before spending oracle calls.
