+        "d=2 zero-excess graph-growth schedule",
+        "slot allocation of vertices",
+    ],
+    "verification_operations": [
+        "exact graph adjacency lookup",
+        "growth-schedule replay",
+        "integer slot and partition comparison",
+    ],
+    "domain_essentiality": "native",
+    "reduction_kind": "paper_licensed",
+    "reduction": (
+        "Section 4, Theorem 1 (zero-excess Graph Growth is NP-complete via "
+        "the join of G with a same-sized clique)"
+    ),
+    "reduction_source": "paper_central",
+    "intuition_type": "reduction recognition",
+    "intuition_description": (
+        "Vertices born together must be independent, so after recognizing the "
+        "paper's universal-clique construction the three final growth slots "
+        "are exactly a proper 3-colouring of the sparse factor; without this "
+        "recognition one searches directly over growth schedules."
+    ),
+    "hardness_basis": (
+        "Track A: Section 4, Theorem 1 proves zero-excess Graph Growth "
+        "NP-complete by reducing colouring to the join G+K_n; shipping uses "
