+# arXiv 2107.14126 — verified graph-growth generator
+
+Status: the generator passes every local gate, but it is **not release-ready**
+because the mandatory OpenRouter hardening and G9 arms could not run: the
+configured key returned HTTP 403 `Key limit exceeded (total limit)` on every
+redraw. No model error has been counted as a failed solve.
+
+| profile field | value |
+|---|---|
+| Track | **A — structural hardness** |
+| native domain | combinatorics |
+| object regime | finite discrete |
+| computational core | CSP/SAT (graph coloring) |
+| certificate | exact symbolic set partition |
+| intuition | reduction recognition |
+| domain essentiality | licensed reduction |
+| reduction | paper-licensed, Section 3, Theorem 4 |
+
+## Problem and trust model
+
+The source is Mertzios et al., [*The Complexity of Growing a
+Graph*](https://arxiv.org/abs/2107.14126). The solver receives a graph `H` and
+the paper's target graph represented exactly as the join of `H` with an
+equally large universal clique. It must partition `H` into a fixed number of
+independent birth slots. The verifier expands that partition into the complete
+`d=2`, zero-excess schedule, replays every birth and locally permitted edge
+activation, and compares the resulting graph with the target using integers
+and bit sets only.
+
+Generation is inverse: a balanced hidden partition is drawn first and edges
+are sampled only across different hidden classes. The stored answer therefore
+exists before the graph does; `make_instance` never colors its own output.
+
+## Why this is the hard regime
+
+Section 2.1 and Definition 1 fix the dynamics. Section 3, Theorem 4 proves the
+zero-excess decision problem NP-complete by exactly the universal-clique join
+used here: the remaining schedule slots encode a coloring of `H`. The following
+theorem rules out an `n^(1/3-epsilon)` approximation unless P=NP. The shipping
+distribution is more specific—balanced planted 6-color graphs with `n=192`
+and cross-class edge probability `0.13`—so the worst-case theorem alone does
+not prove distributional hardness. The empirical basis is that exact DSATUR
+exhausted 100,001 nodes on every one of eight shipping seeds, averaging 3.639 s
+per instance, and the four construction-aware probes also had 0/8 successes.
+
+The easy results were deliberately excluded: Section 2's polynomial trimming
+algorithm solves `d=1`; Section 3's candidate-elimination algorithm recognizes
+unbounded-length zero-excess schedules; and Section 3's matching-plus-2-SAT
+algorithm solves the special case of exactly `log n` zero-excess slots. This
+family uses `d=2` in the variable-slot NP-complete regime.
+
+## Worked demo (`seed=3`)
+
+This is the full rendered instance (the demo is genuinely hand-scale):
+
+```text
+Zero-excess growth schedule for a universal-join graph
+
+There are two named groups of vertices:
+
+* U0,...,U8 form a clique, and every Ui is adjacent to every other
+  vertex. Thus all U-vertices are universal.
+* H0,...,H8 induce the graph H whose complete edge list is printed below.
+  There are no other H-H edges.
+
+The target graph T is exactly this 18-vertex graph. Vertex indices are
+0-based. Every edge [a,b] below is undirected; endpoint order and edge-list
+order carry no information.
+
+H_EDGES=[[1,3],[0,3],[3,8],[2,8],[5,7],[3,5],[2,6],[4,6],[1,7],[7,8],[0,2],[0,6]]
+
+Growth rule (edge-activation distance d=2): initially only U0 exists. In one
+update slot, each already existing vertex may create at most one new child.
+A new child must connect to its parent and may also connect to any already
+existing neighbor of that parent. Two children created in the same slot
+cannot be connected to each other. A zero-excess schedule never deletes an
+edge.
+
+Find exactly 3 nonempty sets partitioning all H-vertex indices 0,...,8 such
+that no H-edge has both endpoints in one set. First create U1,...,U8 one per
+slot from U0, connecting each to all older U-vertices; then use your 3 sets as
+the next 3 birth slots. Within each set, increasing H-index order assigns
+distinct parents U0,U1,..., and every child activates exactly its target edges
+to older vertices. The schedule has at most 11 update slots. Set order and
+order inside a set do not matter, repeats are forbidden, and every H-index
+must occur exactly once.
+
+Give your final answer inside <answer></answer> tags as a JSON list of exactly
+3 nonempty integer lists.
+Example format: <answer>[[0,3],[1,4],[2,5]]</answer>
+Output nothing else inside the tags.
+```
+
+Answer: `<answer>[[0,4,8],[1,5,6],[2,3,7]]</answer>`.
+`verify` returns `(True, "ok")`. Replacing the final `7` with another `0`
+returns `(False, "duplicate vertex: 0")`.
+
+## Difficulty presets
+
+| preset | base vertices | colors | cross-edge probability | status |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---|
+| demo | 9 | 3 | 0.55 | hand-solvable illustration |
+| easy | 192 | 6 | 0.13 | provisional shipping preset; locally validated |
+| medium | 208 | 6 | 0.12 | reserved escalation |
+| hard | 224 | 6 | 0.11 | reserved escalation |
+
+The non-demo rungs keep expected degree near 20 while growing the partition
+space. No preset has been rejected; the oracle ladder never completed its
+first valid attempt.
+
+## Gate results
+
+| gate | result | measurement |
+|---|---|---|
+| G1 | pass | 12/12 planted witnesses; 12/12 JSON-native |
+| G2 | pass | five corruptions rejected with five distinct reasons |
+| G3 | pass | tagged fenced response round-trips; garbage returns `None` |
+| G4 | pass | 0/200,000 structure-aware guesses |
+| G5 | pass | shipping density 0/200,000; demo has 30/3,025 valid partitions; DSATUR 800,008 nodes total |
+| G6 | pass | degree, greedy, 256-restart greedy, spectral, and exact DSATUR all 0/8 |
+| G7 | pass | `n=384` doubled instance builds and replays |
+| G8 | pass | 60/60 invariance and 60/60 carried-witness checks; 20/20 unrelated keys distinct |
+| G9 | **pending** | caps pass (671 chars, 168 estimated tokens, 192 atoms, 198 intended operations); oracle-dependent polarity gate not run |
+
+## Oracle loop and G9
+
+The harness selected the seeds below, but every call was an API error and thus
+consumed no attempt. There is no compliant hardness verdict yet.
+
+| preset | seed | model | solved | reason |
+|---|---:|---|---|---|
+| easy | 109904035 | openai/gpt-5.6-terra | error | HTTP 403 key total limit |
+| easy | 1667670536 | openai/gpt-5.6-terra | error | HTTP 403 key total limit |
+| easy | 493160331 | openai/gpt-5.6-terra | error | HTTP 403 key total limit |
+| easy | 1704206345 | anthropic/claude-sonnet-5 | error | HTTP 403 key total limit |
+
+| G9 arm | solved / valid attempts | conclusion |
+|---|---:|---|
+| bare | 0/0 | not measured |
+| structural hint | 0/0 | not measured; verdict pending |
+| placebo | 0/0 | not measured |
+
+Hinted-minus-placebo is undefined until valid calls exist; the JSON currently
+records `0.0` only because both denominators are zero. Once the key is restored,
+rerun the bare harness and both isolated arms, update `G9_RESULTS`, and rerun
+`selftest()`.
+
+## Use
+
+```python
+import gen_2107_14126 as g
+
+params = g.DIFFICULTY[g.SHIPPING_DIFFICULTY]
+inst = g.make_instance(seed=42, **params)
+question = g.render(inst)
+answer = g.parse_answer("<answer>" + __import__("json").dumps(inst["answer"])
+                        + "</answer>")
+assert g.verify(inst, answer) == (True, "ok")
+```
+
+From the repository root, after valid oracle evidence exists:
+
+```bash
+scripts/emit.sh 2107.14126 20 easy
+```
+
+## Caveats
+
+The NP-completeness theorem is worst-case; it does not certify this planted
+distribution. Zero hits in 200,000 structured samples is an observed rate, not
+a proof that the true density is below `1e-6`. The exact attack is capped at
+100,000 nodes, and the spectral attack is a standard bottom-eigenspace plus
+k-means probe, not an SDP. Belief propagation, stronger SAT/CP-SAT encodings,
+SDP relaxations, and industrial coloring packages were not tested and could
+invalidate the Track A claim. The canonical key uses 1-WL refinement plus cell
+edge counts; it is invariant under the tested relabellings but is not a complete
+graph-isomorphism canonical form. Finally, no release claim should be trusted
+until the required multi-vendor bare, hinted, and placebo runs complete.
