codex
The literature check exposed an important asymptotic flaw in the first draft: a fixed edge probability makes the planted graph denser as `n` grows, entering regimes with known polynomial planted-coloring recovery algorithms. I’m correcting the distribution to fixed expected degree (`p=25/n`, about 20.8 actual expected degree after forbidding same-color edges) before treating Track A as plausible. This keeps the shipping point nearly unchanged but makes the scaling claim honest.
apply patch
