Files:

- [Generator](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2107.14126/gen_2107_14126.py)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2107.14126/selftest_report.json)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2107.14126/README.md)
- [Bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2107.14126/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [Hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2107.14126/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [Placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2107.14126/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

The Track A family uses the paper’s Section 3 coloring-to-growth reduction: a planted coloring expands into an exactly replayable zero-excess growth schedule. The distribution keeps expected degree fixed as size grows, avoiding the obvious dense planted-coloring regime. This distinction matters because polynomial recovery algorithms are known for other planted-coloring regimes. ([source paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2107.14126), [planted-coloring analysis](https://arxiv.org/abs/1603.05183))

Local results:

- G1–G8 pass.
- Structured guesses: 0/200,000.
- Five attacks: 0/8 each.
- Exact DSATUR: 100,001 nodes on every seed, 3.187 seconds mean.
- Answer: 671 characters, 192 atoms.
- G9 remains pending/failing.

All three oracle runs returned HTTP 403 `Key limit exceeded (total limit)`. The transcripts record these as errors, not model failures. Restore the OpenRouter quota and rerun `harden.py` to complete G9 and establish a shipping verdict.
