codex
Implemented and locally verified a Track A generator using the paper’s coloring-to-zero-excess-growth reduction. Step 0 confirmed the polynomial candidate-elimination and \(\log n\) regimes must be avoided, while Theorem 4 supplies the NP-complete regime used here. [Paper PDF](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2107.14126)

Deliverables:

- [gen_2107_14126.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2107.14126/gen_2107_14126.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2107.14126/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2107.14126/README.md)
- [bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2107.14126/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2107.14126/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2107.14126/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

Local results:

- All G1–G9(c) gates pass.
- Random guesses: 0/200,000.
- Five adversarial attacks: all 0/8.
- Exact DSATUR baseline: 800,008 nodes, 33.635 seconds.
- Answer: 671 characters, 192 atoms.
- Canonical-key invariance: 60/60; unrelated keys: 20/20 distinct.

The result is not yet shippable: OpenRouter rejected every hardening and G9 request with HTTP 403 `Key limit exceeded (total limit)` before an oracle ran. The transcripts record these errors, not model failures. Restoring OpenRouter quota and rerunning the three harness arms is the sole remaining step.
